{#
  City skylines as an inline SVG sprite, for the hero card's background.

  Same contract as weather-icons.njk beside it, and for the same reason: the place is upstream
  data, app.js renders with createElement and textContent and never innerHTML, so the shapes live
  in the markup and the script only points a <use> at one of them by id. A place name can
  therefore never become markup.

  **Why drawn rather than a map.** A basemap of where the reader lives would be a tile request
  from the busiest page in the app to a third party, on every load, with nobody having pressed
  anything - and the tile numbers are the location. /privacy/ 3.3 says a map is drawn on two
  pages and names them. These are half a kilobyte of path data each, they fetch nothing, and they
  keep that sentence true.

  **One silhouette, not a row of logos.** Each is a single continuous ground line with the
  landmarks standing on it in roughly their real order, so it reads as a place seen from a
  distance rather than as a sticker sheet. Recognition is the whole point: somebody who knows
  Uppsala should catch the cathedral's twin spires before they notice anything else.

  **Recognition is contrast, and it took two goes to learn that.** The first attempt was typed by
  hand and produced three interchangeable block cities. The second was generated from shape
  primitives, got the landmarks right, and STILL read as one town - because eighteen boxes of
  roughly equal size drown whatever is standing among them. The landmark has to tower over its
  own skyline the way it does in life, and there has to be little enough else for the eye to land
  on it. Uppsala is a low town with one enormous cathedral; Stockholm is a famously even roofline
  with three unmistakable things sticking out of it. Drawing that difference is most of the work.

  1200x200, ground at y=200. `xMidYMax meet` rather than `slice`: meet always shows the whole
  city sitting on the bottom edge, where slice on a wide short card scales to cover and crops
  the top - which is precisely where the spires are. Verified at 1400x230 and at 360x200.

  fill="currentColor" throughout, so one themed class inks the whole drawing. An SVG with hex
  fills in it is a drawing that is unreadable in one of the two modes.
#}
<svg width="0" height="0" class="hidden" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">

  {# A low town with one absurd cathedral, which is what Uppsala actually looks like:
       118 metres of it over five-storey streets. Carolina Rediviva's pediment to its left,
       Gustavianum's little dome to its right, and the castle's long mass with its round tower. #}
  <symbol id="city-uppsala" viewBox="0 0 1200 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet">
    <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 200V194h1200V200z M20 200V182h76V200z M112 200V184l24 -9l24 9V200z M178 200V178h44V200z M252 200V160l56 -15l56 15V200z M392 200V184h30V200z M470 200V88h124V200z M454 200V60h10V48l8 -40l8 40V60h10V200z M578 200V60h10V48l8 -40l8 40V60h10V200z M636 200V184h34V200z M700 200V178a16 17 0 0 1 32 0V200zM714.5 161h3v-8.5h-3z M806 200V166h150V200z M790 200V168a21 21 0 0 1 42 0V200zM809.5 147h3v-10.5h-3z M1004 200V184h46V200z M1076 200V184l22 -9l22 9V200z M1148 200V180h52V200z"/>
  </symbol>

  {# The even cornice line that is the whole character of the inner city, with the three
       things that break it: Stadshuset's tower and its needle, Riddarholmskyrkan's openwork
       spire, Katarina's dome, and Globen - the one perfectly round thing in Stockholm. #}
  <symbol id="city-stockholm" viewBox="0 0 1200 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet">
    <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 200V194h1200V200z M18 200V178h104V200z M140 200V180h92V200z M244 200V178h96V200z M356 200V180h88V200z M486 200V62h16V40h13.5V8h5V40h13.5V62h16V200z M566 200V180h52V200z M648 200V140h13.5V124l7.5 -92l7.5 92V140h13.5V200z M710 200V180h56V200z M788 200V172a33 40 0 0 1 66 0V200zM819.5 132h3v-20h-3z M872 200V180h62V200z M956 118a52 52 0 1 1 104 0a52 52 0 1 1 -104 0zM975 174h66V200h-66z M1100 200V180h70V200z"/>
  </symbol>

  {# Anywhere this does not know. Nothing dominates, deliberately: inventing a landmark
       would be a claim about a place, and a town with no cathedral in it is still a town. #}
  <symbol id="city-generic" viewBox="0 0 1200 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet">
    <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 200V194h1200V200z M24 200V180h84V200z M124 200V182l28 -11l28 11V200z M196 200V172h50V200z M272 200V180h92V200z M384 200V180l31 -12l31 12V200z M500 200V128h12.5V116l7.5 -58l7.5 58V128h12.5V200z M566 200V178h56V200z M646 200V174a23 22 0 0 1 46 0V200zM667.5 152h3v-11h-3z M714 200V182h96V200z M830 200V168h52V200z M908 200V182l30 -11l30 11V200z M996 200V180h76V200z M1092 200V174h48V200z M1160 200V184l20 -9l20 9V200z"/>
  </symbol>

</svg>
